WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.767
-It's Adam Sandler.
It's great to see you.

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.434
-I'm happy to see everybody.
Everybody looks very nice.

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:05.801
You look fantastic.
-Oh, come on, buddy.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:07.501
You look great, too. It's great
you're here in person.

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:09.067
-Yes.
-You helped us out

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.200
during the Zoom shows.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.801
-Of course. That was great.
-I appreciate that.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:15.167
-Oh, by the way,
when we just shook hands.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:18.033
Did we ever --
Isn't it, like, a dilemma

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.300
if you're supposed to shake
or fist bump?

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.067
You ever see three people
you know...

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:27.400
and you hug two and then you go,
"What am I doing?"

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.033
And then the third person,
you give a fist bump,

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:31.367
and then that person
is kind of like,

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:34.067
"Why didn't I get the hug?"

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:38.868
And then you go,
"Oh, 'cause I don't like you."

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:41.667
-I noticed there's something
going on in your eye, buddy.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.601
-I had an accident, everybody.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:46.601
Everything's alright,
but I wish it was a good story.

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.467
It's pathetic.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:51.534
So, what happened was, Jimmy,
I'm in my bed.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:52.901
-Uh-huh.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:54.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.100
Oh, my God. Wow.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.567
-So I -- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I'm in my bed.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:01:01.901
It's 4:00 in the morning.
And somebody made the bed.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:03.434
You know when they make the bed

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.968
and they tuck in
the bottom part of the bed?

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:09.067
So -- So I'm in the bed
and I'm kind of like --

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:10.834
It's 4:00 in the morning.
I forgot to untuck it.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:12.901
I'm going, "Why is it
so uncomfortable here?"

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.334
And I'm feeling squished
and I have --

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:18.300
My phone is here next to me
in the bed.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.734
I always, before I go to sleep,

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:22.334
check out my net worth
on the phone, you know?

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:24.868
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
As one -- As one does.

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:26.200
Yeah, of course.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.667
-You got to know
how life is and all that.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.534
So, anyways, I, for real,

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:34.767
started getting panicky,
and I kicked my legs.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.767
It's like, "Goddamn bed."
And voom --

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:38.334
And the phone flies in the air

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.300
and hits me in the face.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.667
[ Sad tuba ]

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.434
That's so funny.

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:50.367
Anyways,
I was bleeding terribly.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:52.033
I mean, I thought --
It was pitch black in the room,

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.300
and I feel --
and I feel wetness.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.667
And I go, "Yes, I'm --"
I tricked myself.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:59.667
I go, "Those are probably
just thick tears."

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.868
'Cause I really was so tired.

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:04.200
-You cry sometimes
when you sleep?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.334
-Yeah. I was having a sad dream.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:10.634
No. I didn't want to get up,
you know, because I was tired.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:12.534
And I was like,
"Ah, we'll fix that later."

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:14.868
So I slept,
and then I think I took a pillow

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.667
and put it on it
to stop the bleeding.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:20.100
And then when I woke up,
it was horrible.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.601
It was bleeding all over.
It was gushing still and --

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.234
-Blood all over the bed.

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:25.968
-There was blood on the bed
and all that stuff.

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:29.701
And then --
So I went to the -- I said,

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:33.434
"I got to get this fixed,"
so I went to the Apple Store.

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:34.934
-Yeah, you got to get --

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:37.067
Yeah, make sure that worked
and yeah, yeah, yeah. Yeah.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.000
How is the fam?

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.167
I know you have
two beautiful daughters.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:42.934
-As do you.
I saw the pictures of the kids.

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:44.801
They look incredible.
-Thank you, buddy. Yeah.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:45.968
-Gorgeous. Yes.

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:47.834
-How old are your kids now?
-13 and 16.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:51.868
So they had a bat mitzvah and
a sweet 16 on the same weekend.

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:53.434
That was a big deal, right?

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:55.400
Bat mitzvah...
[ Applause ]

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.834
-That's a lot of party.
-It was a big party.

00:02:57.834 --> 00:03:01.000
It was such a giant party we
threw for them, me and my wife,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.534
that I literally had to sign
a new 10-picture deal

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:04.801
with Netflix to pay for it.

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.767
I was like -- I need help, man.

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:08.400
-But I heard that this is
the one that I heard

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.734
Charlie Puth -- Halsey was at
and performed? Come on.

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.601
-Yes. They were awesome.
They were great.

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.367
-That's a good dad.
-Such nice people.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:16.834
-Good mom.
-Yes, yes.

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:19.400
Actually, they --
The kids had the greatest time.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.834
And Halsey and Charlie Puth

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:22.934
were great to them all
and included them.

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:25.934
And the kids sang with them.
And they -- it was beautiful.

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:28.968
But it kind of warped their
heads a little bit thinking,

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:32.000
like, that's what happens
at bat mitzvahs.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.534
And, like, they went to a bat
mitzvah a couple weeks later,

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:38.067
one of my daughter's friends.

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.400
I said,
"How was the bat mitzvah?"

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.434
One of my daughter's friends
said, "Oh, it was lame.

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:43.534
You know,
they didn't have no --

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:49.467
The kid's grandmother
sang karaoke."

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:52.167
I was like, "That's -- You know,
that's actually nice."

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:55.100
You know? And it was actually
Barbra Streisand, too.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.067
-Oh, wow! Hey.
Yeah. They don't know.

00:03:58.067 --> 00:03:59.400
-They didn't know.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:03.934
-You sent over --

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:05.601
You sent over a photo...
-Yes.

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:07.634
-...which I think
this is very sweet.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.367
-This is incredible.
-Tell us about this.

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:11.801
This is your --
-That's my wife's grandma.

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:15.501
106 years old yesterday.
And she's awesome.

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:17.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's amazing.

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:19.367
♪♪

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:22.000
-She's a beautiful,
funny, nice lady.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.567
Always in a good mood.
And just a good, good lady.

00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:27.601
And I love her.
And the whole family loves her.

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.100
-What's she doing here
in this picture?

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.300
-She's pointing -- You see that
she's pointing in that shot?

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:34.033
She's pointing at me saying,
"you'll never live this long."

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:36.501
[ Laughter ]
No, no.

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:38.667
So, I do love her very much.

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:40.300
We all went to see her
in Florida

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.634
and then bought her a cake

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:45.701
and put 106 candles
on the cake for her.

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:47.868
And just to make it fun, I --

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:51.667
The candles were the
Gwyneth Paltrow vagina candles.

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:54.033
So, you know, the "smell
like the vagina" candles?

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:55.434
-Uh-huh.
-So we put them on the cake.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:57.634
-Uh-huh.
-Hang on.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:04:59.534
There's more. There's more.

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:02.801
And, so,
Grandma blows very hard.

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:05.234
-Okay.

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:07.501
-And a lot of smoke in the room.
-Yeah.

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:09.968
-You know? 'Cause she just
put a lot of pizazz

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:13.868
into the blow to get
all 106 vagina candles out.

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:16.100
And then everyone in the room
was pregnant.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.801
-There you go.
That's a great party.

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:20.267
Unbelievable.

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:21.667
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:24.701
-I want to talk about
your fantastic movie "Hustle."

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:26.934
Congrats, bud. I loved it.
-Thank you.

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:28.400
-This movie is --

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.801
It's set in the world
of professional basketball.

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:31.133
-Yes.
-I know you love basketball.

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:33.033
-Yes.
-And LeBron James calls you up

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:34.901
and says,
"Adam, we should do this.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.934
I want to produce this movie
with you."

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:40.501
-His company, LeBron's company,
and Joe Roth,

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:42.434
they had this great script.

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:45.467
And it was about a scout
discovering someone overseas,

00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:47.534
bringing him into the NBA,
and it was awesome.

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:49.934
And I got to know LeBron
a little bit and I asked him --

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:53.067
I do play a lot of hoops,
so I wanted to get a quick tip.

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:56.834
And I said, "Anything
you suggest to fix my game?"

00:05:56.834 --> 00:05:59.701
And he goes, "You should
definitely -- It's very simple.

00:05:59.701 --> 00:06:03.300
You should definitely get
a full body transplant."

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.667
And so I said,
"Yeah, I'm going to do that."

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:06.000
-That's interesting. Yeah.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.133
But that right there,
I would want to see the movie.

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:09.734
LeBron James, Adam Sandler.

00:06:09.734 --> 00:06:12.133
I'm in. I will watch this movie.
I'm so psyched.

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:13.467
-Thank you, man. It's cool.

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:16.167
-And then you get to see
Queen Latifah in the movie.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:17.400
-Your queen.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.133
-That's my --
I love Queen Latifah.

00:06:19.133 --> 00:06:22.367
-What a nice, great lady.
-She's unbelievable.

00:06:22.367 --> 00:06:25.601
-Beautiful. Funny. It's funny.

00:06:25.601 --> 00:06:27.033
She can do so much.

00:06:27.033 --> 00:06:31.801
She can sing, rap,
act, drama, comedy.

00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:33.133
And everyone just loves her.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:34.868
And I said,
"She can do all that."

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:36.968
And you start getting jealous
when you're around that nice.

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:38.334
She can do that,

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:40.934
but can she look like
she hasn't slept in 30 days?

00:06:40.934 --> 00:06:42.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.467
-Hey, you really -- Yeah.
You got to have something.

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:46.634
You got to leave something
for yourself there.

00:06:46.634 --> 00:06:48.300
You know what
I was going to ask?

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.200
Because I know you got some
skills. I've seen some --

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.601
You go to different pickup games
every now and then.

00:06:52.601 --> 00:06:56.300
-So you --
Somebody told me you hooped.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:58.367
When was that?
-This is -- I was in college.

00:06:58.367 --> 00:07:00.133
This is my most famous
story ever.

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:01.467
I retired from playing.

00:07:01.467 --> 00:07:04.300
-What happened? Tell me.
-I'm in Albany, New York.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.767
I was in college.
Saint Rose. Walked down.

00:07:06.767 --> 00:07:08.234
There was a pickup game at --

00:07:08.234 --> 00:07:09.501
I can't say the name
of the park.

00:07:09.501 --> 00:07:13.033
S-Talkers Park.
-Okay. Okay. I got you.

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:14.634
-S-Talkers Park.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:17.300
I go there, and I'm just
playing a pickup game

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:18.601
with my friend Danny Martinez.

00:07:18.601 --> 00:07:20.601
And we're going...

00:07:20.601 --> 00:07:24.434
And there's maybe 30 kids around
the court watching the game,

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:27.868
rooting for everybody,
and one of the hoops is bent.

00:07:27.868 --> 00:07:30.067
So you can --
The rim's a little --

00:07:30.067 --> 00:07:32.601
You could dunk it
if there's no one there.

00:07:32.601 --> 00:07:36.367
And I practiced and did it --
I could dunk the basketball.

00:07:36.367 --> 00:07:38.167
-That's sick.
-Yeah. It was pretty cool.

00:07:38.167 --> 00:07:39.834
But I would never do it
in a real game.

00:07:39.834 --> 00:07:41.767
-Right, right, right.
-So I'm playing the game.

00:07:41.767 --> 00:07:43.734
There's people in --
I'm terrible.

00:07:43.734 --> 00:07:46.234
And I'm just bad.
I'm sweating and everything.

00:07:46.234 --> 00:07:48.801
And I'm just --
I have weird moves and stuff.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:51.300
I have a move where I can --
I can foul you with this hand

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.901
and then air-hook it.

00:07:53.901 --> 00:07:56.767
And it never goes in,
but it looked cool, you know?

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:59.334
So I'm doing this thing
and I steal the ball

00:07:59.334 --> 00:08:01.300
and I get a fast break.
-Uh-huh.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.734
-And it just, like, starts
going in slow motion,

00:08:03.734 --> 00:08:05.200
and I'm like...

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:09.434
And my fat is jiggling around
and sweat coming off. I go --

00:08:09.434 --> 00:08:10.901
And everyone's going like,

00:08:10.901 --> 00:08:12.968
"There's no way this dude
is gonna dunk this ball."

00:08:12.968 --> 00:08:15.400
But it's the rim
that's pulled down.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.634
It's very possible.
And I go...

00:08:17.634 --> 00:08:18.901
[ Laughter ]

00:08:18.901 --> 00:08:22.434
And I'm like, "Don't travel.
Don't travel."

00:08:22.434 --> 00:08:26.267
One, two. Ga-doosh!

00:08:26.267 --> 00:08:29.100
I dunk the ball. People go nuts.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.601
They lift me up. I'm like Rudy.

00:08:32.601 --> 00:08:35.067
They take me home. You know?

00:08:35.067 --> 00:08:36.901
And I retired
from playing basketball.

00:08:36.901 --> 00:08:38.968
-That's unbelievable.
-Yeah.

00:08:38.968 --> 00:08:42.901
My friend Ralphie Salazar
is my --

00:08:42.901 --> 00:08:44.334
He knows that it happened.
-He saw that.

00:08:44.334 --> 00:08:46.767
-He saw it. He really knows
it happened for real.

00:08:46.767 --> 00:08:48.067
-That's amazing.

00:08:48.067 --> 00:08:49.434
-It's the best thing
that ever happened to me.

00:08:49.434 --> 00:08:50.801
I retired. I couldn't --
I couldn't believe it.

00:08:50.801 --> 00:08:52.300
I couldn't ever go back.
-Can you believe you got up

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.100
that high,
even if the rim was bent?

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.701
-You know, I thought maybe
I should go back in a disguise

00:08:56.701 --> 00:08:58.868
and just, like,
look back at the court.

00:08:58.868 --> 00:09:01.734
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]
And feel that moment again.

00:09:01.734 --> 00:09:04.567
-Yeah, yeah. Like "Eddie
an the Cruisers," you know?

00:09:04.567 --> 00:09:06.234
-Yeah, man.
-"Oh, he's a legend.

00:09:06.234 --> 00:09:07.801
He doesn't exist."

00:09:07.801 --> 00:09:09.868
-Oh, man. Yeah.

00:09:09.868 --> 00:09:12.868
-But did you ever have a story
like that?

00:09:12.868 --> 00:09:14.234
Did you ever dunk it?

00:09:14.234 --> 00:09:17.000
-Dude, I literally --
I've never in my whole life

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.501
came close to the rim.

00:09:18.501 --> 00:09:20.667
Everybody talks about
touching the rim,

00:09:20.667 --> 00:09:22.200
and I can't even
get the backboard.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.534
I can't even like -- When
I hit the bottom of the net,

00:09:24.534 --> 00:09:27.267
I'm kind of like,
"I got the net."

00:09:27.267 --> 00:09:29.000
I know. It's pathetic.
I don't know why.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.400
I just can't jump.
I'm so slow, too.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.834
I remember when I was
in Little League baseball,

00:09:34.834 --> 00:09:37.567
I thought I was so fast.

00:09:37.567 --> 00:09:38.968
Because I tried so hard.

00:09:38.968 --> 00:09:40.300
I hit a ball.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.400
I'm running to first as fa--

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:44.601
You know, like, I never knew
how to pump my arms.

00:09:44.601 --> 00:09:47.133
I was like, "Do you do your
hands like this or like this?"

00:09:47.133 --> 00:09:50.300
And I was just like --
And I remember seeing my dugout.

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:52.434
All the kids just
laughing and laughing.

00:09:52.434 --> 00:09:54.501
I was like, "Oh, they're
laughing in excitement

00:09:54.501 --> 00:09:56.934
of how fast
I'm going right now."

00:09:56.934 --> 00:09:58.534
I came back, I was like,
"What happened?"

00:09:58.534 --> 00:10:00.868
They were like,
"What the hell?!

00:10:00.868 --> 00:10:03.300
How do you run that slow?!"

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:06.133
I was like..."I run slow?"

00:10:06.133 --> 00:10:08.534
-"I was going normal."

00:10:08.534 --> 00:10:10.667
-There was no video cameras
back there

00:10:10.667 --> 00:10:12.300
showing you how goofy you were.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.000
I literally thought
I was incredible at everything.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.701
-Well, I have a video
that someone shot of you

00:10:16.701 --> 00:10:18.901
doing something spectacular.

00:10:18.901 --> 00:10:21.701
Take a look at Adam Sandler
making a balcony shot.

00:10:21.701 --> 00:10:23.767
-Oh, okay. Yes, yes.
-Look at this thing.

00:10:23.767 --> 00:10:25.501
-My name is Adam Sandler,

00:10:25.501 --> 00:10:28.334
and you are watching
Balcony Ball.

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:33.701
-Ohh!

00:10:33.701 --> 00:10:36.133
♪♪

00:10:36.133 --> 00:10:38.467
-...carry you. I want to carry
you around like Rudy!

00:10:38.467 --> 00:10:40.234
I want to carry you around
like Rudy!

00:10:40.234 --> 00:10:41.701
That's what I'm talking about.
-You can't lift me.

00:10:41.701 --> 00:10:43.667
-Yeah, I can. I want
to talk more about "Hustle"

00:10:43.667 --> 00:10:45.133
and show a clip
when we come back.

00:10:45.133 --> 00:10:46.634
More with Adam Sandler,
everybody.

00:10:46.634 --> 00:10:48.300
That's how you do it.

